#!/bin/bash

# DELIBERATELY DOES NOT ACTIVATE DEVBOX.
#
# The devbox shell IS the isolated environment: inside it $HOME is sealed to
# .aihome/ and every tool reads workspace config. Outside it you are on the host,
# with your own git identity, credentials and shell — exactly as you'd expect
# standing in any other directory.
#
# direnv's `use devbox` collapses that distinction. It evaluates
# `devbox shellenv --init-hook` and exports the whole env into your CURRENT
# shell, so merely `cd`-ing here would seal you without your having entered
# anything. That cost this workspace its ability to commit from a normal shell
# once HOME moved into the box.
#
# So: entering is an explicit act.
#
#     devbox shell        -> inside the box (sealed)
#     exit                -> back on the host
#     devbox run <verb>   -> runs that verb inside the box
#
# If you re-add `use devbox` below, `cd` will silently seal your shell again.
# Don't — see [01] system/SYSTEM-RULES.md Rule 8.
